   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You have 140 ft of fencing to enclose a rectangular region that borders a river. You do not have to fence in the side that borders the river. The width is equal to <span data-math=\"2a\">2a</span>, and the length is equal to six times the width less 10. Find the dimensions of the region to be fenced.<br>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b51608fb5390fdd3.png\" alt=\"A fence has borders on three sides. The fourth side bordering a river does not have a fence. The left and right sides measure 2 a. The bottom side measures 6 a minus 10.\">\n",
